# This repository's working tree is the WHOLE HOME DIRECTORY (C:\Users\kenda), and its
# remote is github.com/getcotto/cotto-site. Only three paths are actually part of the
# project: .gitignore, cotto-site/ and ops/ (139 files).
#
# Everything else in here is Kendall's personal machine: Dropbox/, OneDrive/, Documents/,
# Downloads/, AppData/, .claude/ (which holds credentials and memory), .gitconfig,
# NTUSER.DAT. None of it was ignored, so a single `git add -A` run from the home
# directory would have staged all of it for a push to GitHub. Nothing has leaked; the
# only thing that prevented it was that nobody happened to run that command.
#
# So: deny by default, then re-allow the project. Added 2026-09-12 during the system
# reconciliation. If you add a new top-level project folder, it needs a `!` line here
# or git will not see it.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/cotto-site/
!/ops/

# Money feeds: real transaction data, never committed.
ops/spine/mercury_transactions.csv
ops/spine/settle_invoices.csv

# Build output and secrets.
.vercel
.env*
